# compose.service.yaml.schema
#
# Companion document for `compose.service.yaml`, the harness layer's deployment
# delta. It is applied **on top of** the agent host's own fragment, which keeps
# owning the agent tree, the agent ids, the supervision and the SSH posture.
#
# ## What this file changes, and what it does not
#
# | Setting | Value | Why |
# |---|---|---|
# | `image` | the harness layer's image | The only change the layer needs at run time: the image already carries the CLI, its configuration and `AGENT_HARNESS`. |
# | `entrypoint` | `sops exec-env … agent-host-boot` | The credential path. The image's own entrypoint is untouched; this starts the boot program explicitly, wrapped so the dotenv entries are decrypted in memory and injected into the harness's environment. |
# | `SOPS_AGE_KEY_FILE` | the mounted key path | Where sops reads the service's dedicated private key. Never the master key. |
# | `secrets` | the encrypted dotenv file and this service's key file | File-backed secrets, mounted read-only. The target of the encrypted store must keep the `.env` suffix: its format is inferred from the extension. |
# | `ports` | absent | The harness is a foreground process in an outbound-only container. Nothing here opens a listener (R-10). |
# | `volumes` | commented | The harness home (`P-9`), optionally. Mounted, session state survives a recreate; unmounted, a recreate starts clean. The mount must be owned by the base image's account or the CLI cannot write session state (Open question Q-1). |
#
# ## Nothing about the harness appears in `environment:`
#
# `AGENT_HARNESS`, the config root and the configuration itself are build-time
# values written into the image. A deployment supplies the alias when it *builds*
# the layer, not when it starts it; that is why this file has no harness
# variables beyond the secrets wrapper's own.
#
# ## The credential variable's name
#
# The harness reads the credential from one variable, and which one is recorded
# inside the image at `/usr/local/share/agent-harness/credential-env`: the layer's
# `ROUTER_CREDENTIAL_ENV` for the Codex harness, `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` for the
# Claude harness (whose configuration names no credential variable at all). The
# encrypted dotenv store must therefore carry the credential under **that** name,
# or the harness starts with no credential and fails its first request.
#
# ## Validation
#
# ```
# docker compose -f <agent host>/compose.service.yaml -f compose.service.yaml config
# docker inspect <container> --format '{{range .Mounts}}{{.Source}} -> {{.Destination}}{{println}}{{end}}'
# docker inspect <container> --format '{{json .NetworkSettings.Ports}}'   # no published port
# ```
